---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "Best Dog Treadmills for Small Dogs (2026): Sized for Toy & Small Breeds";
const description =
  "Four dog treadmills for toy and small breeds sold on Amazon, checked in November 2026: running length against your dog, speed, side panels, what was actually in stock, and the safety rules that matter most.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "gopet-petrun-pr700",
    name: "GoPet PetRun PR700 Dog Treadmill",
    brand: "GoPet",
    category: "Best dog treadmill for toy breeds",
    badge: "Best Overall",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B006GR9FYS?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/417fYDQUjGL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$590 at two US dealers (5 Nov 2026); $851.92 on Amazon (9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":590,"high":851.92},
    specs: "28 x 16 in. running surface · 0.6–8 mph · for dogs up to 44 lb · 1-year warranty",
    pros: [
      "Built as a dog treadmill for toy breeds, with side panels and a low starting speed",
      "Two US dealers agree on its size, speed range and price, and listed it in stock",
      "Compact enough for an apartment, at about 46 by 23 inches overall",
      "Adjustable incline for a vet-directed programme, if you need it",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 28-inch running surface suits only dogs up to about 14 inches nose to base of tail",
      "Not returnable once shipped, with a $300 cancellation fee, at Canine Athletes, and much dearer on Amazon than at the dealers",
      "Only a one-year warranty",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The treadmill to buy for a toy breed, if your dog measures up to about 14 inches from nose to base of tail and you accept the no-returns terms.",
    description: "The PR700 is GoPet’s toy-breed treadmill, and on 5 November 2026 it was the only dog treadmill at Canine Athletes, the main US specialist dealer, marked for toy breeds. Canine Athletes and FactoryPure agree on a 28 by 16-inch running surface, speeds from 0.6 to 8 mph, a one-year warranty and a $590 price; both list a maximum dog weight of 44 lb, though FactoryPure’s overview says 45 lb. Canine Athletes adds an overall size of 46 by 23 by 11 inches, a unit weight of 63 lb and an adjustable “Air Step” incline without a stated range. Canine Athletes marked it very low in stock and FactoryPure in stock, shipping direct from GoPet in five to seven business days by freight. Walmart’s listing showed it higher, at $724.24 plus shipping. GoPet treadmills are not returnable once shipped at Canine Athletes, which charges a $300 cancellation fee, so measure your dog before ordering: 28 inches is right for a Chihuahua, Yorkie or toy poodle, and short for a Dachshund. Amazon also lists the PR700, for dogs up to 44 lb by its title, at $851.92 on 9 November 2026; that is about $260 more than the dealers charged, so check who the seller is and what its returns terms are before choosing Amazon for the convenience.",
  },
  {
    id: "gymax-dog-treadmill-2hp",
    name: "GYMAX Dog Treadmill for Small/Medium Dogs (2HP)",
    brand: "GYMAX",
    category: "Best budget dog treadmill for small dogs",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08ZK6JR2R?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41zYxI9HmqL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $180 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":180,"high":180},
    specs: "0.5–7.5 mph · 2 HP motor · 220 lb maximum load · removable side panels · remote control · 3 incline levels",
    pros: [
      "A fraction of the price of a specialist small-dog treadmill",
      "A 0.5 mph minimum speed, the genuine amble a small or nervous dog needs to start at",
      "Fabric side panels and a remote, so you can stop the belt from beside the dog",
      "The same speed, motor and load figures Costway gives for its own small-dog treadmill",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The Amazon listing does not give the belt length; Costway’s matching model is 39 inches, which suits small dogs only",
      "A 2-in-1 design that converts to a walking pad, so it is not purpose-built for dogs",
      "Load and “pet weight” figures are far beyond what a short belt can accommodate; go by length",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The machine to try first on a budget, for a small dog that fits a belt of about 39 inches: measure your dog, confirm the belt length with the seller and know the return terms before ordering.",
    description: "Costway's own small-and-medium dog treadmill, which an earlier version of this card showed, is sold on Costway's store rather than on Amazon, so this card shows the GYMAX machine Amazon sells; GYMAX is one of Costway's family of brands. The GYMAX listing describes a 2 HP motor running under 45 dB, a 0.5 to 7.5 mph speed range, three incline levels, a 220 lb load, fabric side covers fixed with hook-and-loop, a detachable handlebar, an LCD, a remote that works from about 33 feet and built-in wheels. Those figures match the ones Costway and FactoryPure give for Costway's own machine: a 39 by 15.5-inch belt, 0.5 to 7.5 mph, 2 HP and 220 lb, with a 365-day warranty and 30-day returns on Costway's store. We could not confirm from GYMAX that the Amazon unit is the same machine, so confirm the belt length with the seller; 39 inches suits dogs up to about 19 inches from nose to base of tail, which covers toy and many small breeds but not long-backed ones. Some Costway listings give 1.5 HP rather than 2 HP, and Costway's recommended pet weight of 130 lb is meaningless for a belt this short; go by length. Unlike the GoPet, it is a 2-in-1 that also works as a walking pad. Amazon listed it at $179.99 on 9 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "lifepro-pawrunner",
    name: "Lifepro PawRunner",
    brand: "Lifepro",
    category: "Whole Dog Journal’s 2026 pick for small dogs",
    badge: "Out of Stock at Target",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09M36RXMV?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51gyWO2oB-L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "Not confirmed in stock on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: null,
    specs: "Motorised dog treadmill · side rails · safety key · remote",
    pros: [
      "Named best for small dogs in Whole Dog Journal’s January 2026 comparison",
      "A lifetime limited warranty, according to Target’s listing",
      "Quiet, according to the maker and to reviewers",
      "Less than half the price of the GoPet PR720F",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Out of stock at Target, and sold out at Woot, on the day we checked",
      "Marketed for dogs up to 130 lb; Whole Dog Journal says it suits dogs under about 25 to 30 lb",
      "Deck length and top speed differ between sources",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Worth buying if you find it in stock from a seller with clear returns terms, for a small dog under about 25 lb with a short stride.",
    description: "The PawRunner is Lifepro’s motorised pet treadmill, and Whole Dog Journal’s January 2026 comparison names it the best choice for small dogs, with a caveat we agree with: Lifepro markets it for dogs up to 130 lb, which WDJ calls a little misleading, judging it suitable for dogs under about 25 to 30 lb with short strides. WDJ gives a 42-inch deck and a list price of $400, noting it has sold for as little as $266. Target’s listing, sold by Lifepro, gave $399.99, a lifetime limited warranty, speeds up to 12 mph and an overall size of 48 by 22.8 by 42 inches, but showed it out of stock on 5 November 2026; a retailer description gives the top speed as 7.5 mph instead, and Woot’s listing was sold out. Lifepro’s own site would not load for us, so we have printed no deck size or price on the card. Lifepro Fitness’s one CPSC recall, of infrared sauna blankets in 2025, does not concern this machine.",
  },
  {
    id: "gymax-dog-treadmill-243",
    name: "GYMAX Dog Treadmill (243 lb)",
    brand: "GYMAX",
    category: "Budget dog treadmill with a longer belt",
    badge: "Longer Belt, Low Price",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H2HJVR1R?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41+Nl44d7kL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $190 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":190,"high":190},
    specs: "2.5 HP motor · 0.6–6 mph · 15 preset programs · 243 lb limit · remote control · adjustable incline",
    pros: [
      "A 41 by 16-inch running area by one retailer’s listing, a little longer than the 39 inches of the GYMAX 2 HP’s Costway twin",
      "Starts at 0.6 mph, and a remote lets you stand beside the dog",
      "About a fifth of the price of GoPet’s dealer-only PR720F",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Its running-area size comes from one retailer listing; the Amazon title does not give it",
      "A 243 lb limit that, like Costway’s, says nothing about which dogs fit; go by length",
      "From the same Costway family of brands as the budget card above, with no independent review we could find",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A budget option for a small dog slightly too long for the 2 HP GYMAX, if you confirm the belt length on the listing before ordering.",
    description: "GoPet’s PR720F, the obvious step up from the PR700 for longer small dogs, is sold through dealers rather than on Amazon and was not confirmed in stock, so this card is the longest-belt budget dog treadmill we could check on Amazon. GYMAX is one of Costway’s brands, and its 243 lb dog treadmill is a different model from the 2 HP GYMAX above. The Amazon listing gives a 243 lb limit, a remote, adjustable incline and preset programs; a Best Buy Canada listing for the GYMAX dog treadmill with the same 243 lb limit gives a 2.5 HP motor, 0.6 to 6 mph, 15 preset programs and a 41 by 16-inch running area, and an Amazon listing for the same machine under Costway’s PETSITE brand gives the same motor, speeds, programs and limit. Forty-one inches suits small dogs up to about 20 inches from nose to base of tail, which is longer than the 2 HP GYMAX’s 39-inch Costway twin allows but well short of the PR720F’s 52 inches, so a Corgi or Beagle may still need the GoPet. We found no independent review, so confirm the belt length on the listing you buy from. Amazon listed it at $189.99 on 9 November 2026.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Dog Treadmills for Small Dogs", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-dog-treadmills-for-small-dogs/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What size treadmill does a small dog need?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Measure your dog from the tip of the nose to the base of the tail and double it. That is the minimum running length under the widely used rule of thumb, so a dog measuring 14 inches needs about 28 inches and a 20-inch Dachshund about 40 inches. Ignore the weight rating as a size guide; small-dog machines are often rated for far heavier dogs than they fit.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best doggie treadmill for small dogs?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For toy breeds, the GoPet PetRun PR700, with a 28 by 16-inch running surface and speeds from 0.6 mph, was in stock at $590 from two US dealers on 5 November 2026. Amazon also lists the PR700, at a higher price. For longer small dogs, GoPet’s PR720F, at about 52 inches, is the step up if you can find it in stock at a dealer. On a budget, GYMAX’s 2 HP small-dog machine was about $180 on Amazon, and GYMAX’s longer 243 lb model about $190.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can a small dog use a human treadmill or walking pad?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Some can, at a slow walk and under close supervision, because a small dog needs less belt length. But human machines have no side panels, start faster than many small dogs like and have controls out of your reach while you stand beside the dog. A dog treadmill is designed around those problems. Our guide to dogs on human treadmills sets out the rules if you try.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a motorized dog treadmill safe for a small dog?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It can be, with supervision. Never tether the dog, never leave it alone on a moving belt, start at the lowest speed with you beside it and the remote in your hand, and stop at the first sign of distress. Ask your vet first, especially for puppies, older dogs, flat-faced breeds and dogs with back or knee problems.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the dogPACER MiniPacer still available?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "We could not find it in stock from a US seller on 5 November 2026. Canine Athletes’ product page for it no longer opened, Ray Allen’s link led to a general category page, and dogpacer.com returned a server error. A marketplace copy of a dogPACER listing from May 2026 still showed the full-size LF 3.1 in stock. Check with a seller before relying on any dogPACER model.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long should a small dog walk on a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Start with a few minutes at a slow walk and build up over several weeks, watching the dog rather than the clock. Your vet can suggest a target for your dog’s age, breed and health. A treadmill session adds to walks rather than replacing them.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 4,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-dog-treadmills-for-small-dogs/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-dog-treadmills-for-small-dogs/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "dog treadmill for small dogs",
      "doggie treadmill for small dogs",
      "small dog treadmill",
      "motorized dog treadmill",
      "treadmill for toy breeds",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: GoPet PetRun PR700 Dog Treadmill", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Dog Treadmills for Small Dogs Sized for Toy and Small Breeds</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        A small dog needs less belt than a big one, which widens the choice, and slower, finer speed control, which narrows it again. Here are four motorised dog treadmills sold on Amazon that suit toy and small breeds, what was really in stock on 5 November 2026, how to size one against your dog, and the rules that keep a small dog safe on a moving belt.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#gopet-petrun-pr700"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/417fYDQUjGL._SL500_.jpg" alt="GoPet PetRun PR700 Dog Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#gymax-dog-treadmill-2hp"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41zYxI9HmqL._SL500_.jpg" alt="GYMAX Dog Treadmill for Small/Medium Dogs (2HP)" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#lifepro-pawrunner"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51gyWO2oB-L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Lifepro PawRunner" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>GoPet PetRun PR700 Dog Treadmill · GYMAX Dog Treadmill for Small/Medium Dogs (2HP) · Lifepro PawRunner</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Most of the well-known dog treadmills are built around medium and large dogs, and a Chihuahua,
          a Dachshund or a Jack Russell on one of them is a small dog on a lot of machine. This is the
          small-breed companion to our general <a href="/best-dog-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">dog treadmill roundup</a> and
          our <a href="/best-dog-treadmills-for-large-dogs/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">large-dog guide</a>:
          machines short enough to fit a small home, slow enough to start a nervous dog, and long enough,
          once you have measured, for your dog to walk naturally.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#gopet-petrun-pr700">GoPet PetRun PR700 Dog Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Budget:</span> <a href="#gymax-dog-treadmill-2hp">GYMAX Dog Treadmill for Small/Medium Dogs (2HP)</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Out of Stock at Target:</span> <a href="#lifepro-pawrunner">Lifepro PawRunner</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Longer Belt, Low Price:</span> <a href="#gymax-dog-treadmill-243">GYMAX Dog Treadmill (243 lb)</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below, and what this page is not.</strong> We have not tested these dog treadmills. On 5 November 2026 we checked each against the pages we
          could read: Canine Athletes and FactoryPure (both GoPet dealers) for the GoPet PR700, Costway’s own
          store and a second retailer listing for Costway’s small-dog machine, Target’s listing and Whole Dog
          Journal’s January 2026 comparison for the Lifepro PawRunner, EntirelyPets for the GoPet PR720F, and
          Canine Athletes for the Dog Runner Tracks; neither of the last two is sold on Amazon, so they are
          covered in the text rather than on cards. On 9 November 2026 we added the PR700’s Amazon listing, replaced the Costway card
          with the matching GYMAX 2 HP machine Amazon sells (its figures are those checked for our general
          dog treadmill guide), and checked the 243 lb GYMAX card against its Amazon listing, a Best Buy Canada listing and a PETSITE-branded
          Amazon listing of the same machine. GoPet’s and dogPACER’s own websites would not load for
          us that day, and Amazon’s pages returned errors; the two Amazon prices here were added on 9 November. A figure
          appears in a product’s specification line only where two sources agree; where they disagreed — on
          running length, speed or the weight a machine suits — we left it out and say so in the text. Where
          we could not confirm a machine was in stock, its card says so and carries no price. We searched the
          CPSC recall database for GoPet, Lifepro, Costway, Dog Runner and dogPACER and found no recall of a
          dog treadmill (Lifepro’s and Costway’s recalls were of unrelated products). Prices change often, and
          some of these machines ship by freight and cannot be returned once dispatched, so confirm price,
          stock, warranty and returns with the seller before ordering. This page is about equipment, not
          veterinary advice: speak to your vet before putting any dog on any treadmill, and stop at the first
          sign of distress, lameness, overheating or laboured breathing. We earn a commission if you buy
          through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change which products we list or what we say
          about them.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#quick-picks">Our Picks at a Glance</a></li>
            <li><a href="#picks">The 4 Best Dog Treadmills for Small Dogs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-we-chose">How We Chose These Small-Dog Treadmills</a></li>
            <li><a href="#sizing-small-dogs">Sizing: Running Length Against Your Dog’s Length</a></li>
            <li><a href="#speed-and-controls">Speed, Side Panels and Controls for a Small Dog</a></li>
            <li><a href="#motorized-or-slatmill">Motorised Treadmill or Slatmill for a Small Dog?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#small-dog-health">Small Dogs, Puppies and Older Dogs: Talk to the Vet First</a></li>
            <li><a href="#safety">Safety: Never Tether, Always Supervise</a></li>
            <li><a href="#space-and-delivery">Space, Delivery and the Terms You Sign Up To</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="quick-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Our Picks at a Glance</h2>
<p>
            Four motorised machines, each with a listing on Amazon. The GoPet PR700 is the machine we would
            buy first and is sold on Amazon as well as by specialist dealers, at a higher price there. GoPet’s
            longer PR720F and Dog Runner’s compact Tracks are sold only through dealers, not on Amazon, and
            neither was confirmed in stock, so we cover them in the text and the fourth card is a budget
            machine with a longer belt that Amazon does sell. The PawRunner could not be confirmed in stock at
            Target; its card says so. Match the running length to your dog first.
            If you are still deciding whether your dog needs its own machine at all, read our comparison of <a href="/dog-treadmill-vs-human-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">dog and human treadmills</a> first.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[480px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Pick</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Best for</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Why</th>
              </tr>
